1
00:00:08,560 --> 00:00:11,140
Brighten up the room and try stepping back a little,
won't you?

2
00:00:20,280 --> 00:00:24,260
If you're broke, come on over to my place!

3
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:28,960
I'm broke too, but don't you worry!

4
00:00:28,960 --> 00:00:32,820
Look at the blue sky!

5
00:00:33,840 --> 00:00:36,320
White clouds.

6
00:00:37,740 --> 00:00:42,820
Somehow, it'll all work out eventually.

7
00:00:55,880 --> 00:00:59,900
If you're out of work,
come on over to my place!

8
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:04,540
I've got nothing either,
but don't you worry!

9
00:01:06,320 --> 00:01:12,140
Even the burning steel clusters...

10
00:01:13,500 --> 00:01:18,260
Somehow, it'll all work out eventually.

11
00:01:20,320 --> 00:01:23,540
You get it, right? Got it, got it.

12
00:01:23,540 --> 00:01:27,460
Once you understand,
just keep quiet and follow me!

13
00:01:46,340 --> 00:01:47,800
What an amazing robot.

14
00:01:48,720 --> 00:01:51,420
Is this the latest humanoid robot?

15
00:01:51,880 --> 00:01:53,400
Its movements are so smooth.

16
00:01:54,220 --> 00:01:56,480
Back in the day,
when it came to imitating robots,

17
00:01:59,140 --> 00:02:00,240
Clank!

18
00:02:02,100 --> 00:02:03,360
Clank!

19
00:02:03,360 --> 00:02:04,700
Clank!

20
00:02:04,700 --> 00:02:05,180
Yeah, yeah.

21
00:02:06,320 --> 00:02:10,800
Robots were kind of a joke,
but they've come a long way

22
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:13,260
They're making progress on
practical applications, right?

23
00:02:14,900 --> 00:02:19,680
I heard some fire stations have already
deployed robots that work at actual fire scenes.

24
00:02:20,060 --> 00:02:24,460
One of these days,
we may leave all dangerous jobs to robots.

25
00:02:24,460 --> 00:02:30,620
Maybe a robot cop will show up someday.
Wait, there already was one, the robot cop!

26
00:02:31,360 --> 00:02:33,040
Prototype No. 001.

27
00:02:33,600 --> 00:02:35,580
That was a useless robot.

28
00:02:37,440 --> 00:02:39,760
Robot cops are the real deal now.

29
00:02:40,380 --> 00:02:41,180
Right?

30
00:02:41,180 --> 00:02:42,340
Definitely.

31
00:02:44,860 --> 00:02:46,060
Everyone, rejoice!

32
00:02:46,060 --> 00:02:50,820
A state-of-the-art robot cop is going
to be assigned to this police box!

33
00:02:53,440 --> 00:02:55,500
Chief, what did you just say?

34
00:02:55,960 --> 00:02:59,200
I said the latest model robot
police officer is coming here.

35
00:03:00,620 --> 00:03:01,620
It's Unit 004.

36
00:03:03,040 --> 00:03:04,880
What's wrong? Aren't you happy?

37
00:03:05,260 --> 00:03:06,740
Of course I'm not happy.

38
00:03:07,140 --> 00:03:11,040
I bet some outdated junk
like Unit 001 is coming.

39
00:03:12,940 --> 00:03:14,120
You're naive, Ryotsu.

40
00:03:14,120 --> 00:03:18,080
This time,
we've learned from our past experience

41
00:03:18,700 --> 00:03:20,580
and mobilized 2,000 researchers,

42
00:03:20,580 --> 00:03:24,340
and built it using 3,000
cutting-edge technologies.

43
00:03:26,460 --> 00:03:27,100
And then...

44
00:03:28,840 --> 00:03:29,760
Something like this?

45
00:03:30,620 --> 00:03:32,480
This time, it transforms into a car,
or something like that.

46
00:03:35,620 --> 00:03:37,880
Maybe it's not humanoid after all.

47
00:03:39,540 --> 00:03:42,680
Looks like we're getting a really amazing robot this time,
Ryo-san.

48
00:03:42,680 --> 00:03:46,020
No, I won't be relieved
until I see it in person.

49
00:03:47,340 --> 00:03:49,980
Don't go falling on your butt when you see it in person,
Ryo-san.

50
00:03:51,240 --> 00:03:55,840
This was built by 2,000 researchers
and 3,000 cutting-edge technologies,

51
00:03:55,840 --> 00:03:59,720
the latest model of robot police officer,
Development Unit 004, Otsu model!

52
00:04:00,620 --> 00:04:03,300
Hello, I'm Development Unit 004, Otsu model.

53
00:04:06,180 --> 00:04:08,680
Well, are you too amazed to speak?

54
00:04:08,680 --> 00:04:10,520
Th-this is...

55
00:04:10,980 --> 00:04:12,020
Latest model?

56
00:04:12,520 --> 00:04:15,300
It somehow has a strangely
human atmosphere, though.

57
00:04:15,900 --> 00:04:18,900
Wait, isn't there something inside it?

58
00:04:19,060 --> 00:04:20,360
H-hey, Myō!

59
00:04:20,440 --> 00:04:21,620
It's definitely a robot.

60
00:04:22,520 --> 00:04:22,920
Hey

61
00:04:22,920 --> 00:04:23,860
Of course!

62
00:04:24,520 --> 00:04:30,380
It's the latest robot police officer, built by 2,000
researchers using 3,000 cutting-edge technologies!

63
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:33,680
But that design sense is so outdated

64
00:04:34,320 --> 00:04:36,600
Above all, this design is

65
00:04:36,600 --> 00:04:41,640
a compilation of the greatest common
factor of ideas from 1,000 famous designers!

66
00:04:42,160 --> 00:04:46,720
In other words, it's the most
cutting-edge design of the 21st century!

67
00:04:46,720 --> 00:04:49,320
Just lumping everything together doesn't make it good,
you know.

68
00:04:49,320 --> 00:04:52,020
I'm sure what's inside is amazing.

69
00:04:52,020 --> 00:04:52,600
Yeah, you're right.

70
00:04:53,860 --> 00:04:56,000
Count on you, 004!

71
00:04:57,060 --> 00:04:58,280
Yes, I'll do my best!

72
00:05:01,020 --> 00:05:09,580
Senpai, what should we do? If we have it do something carelessly and it breaks down,
we'll just get an earful from the Chief.

73
00:05:09,960 --> 00:05:16,920
Forget it. I came here to work, so please let me do something.
Fine, fine, fine.

74
00:05:17,560 --> 00:05:21,240
It really is like a human.
It must be because it's the latest model.

75
00:05:22,800 --> 00:05:24,900
So, what can you do?

76
00:05:25,680 --> 00:05:27,960
Yes, I've memorized all the laws.

77
00:05:27,960 --> 00:05:29,840
What about working at the police box?

78
00:05:30,360 --> 00:05:33,720
No, I was told to learn that on the job.

79
00:05:34,280 --> 00:05:36,220
You're a complete rookie officer,
aren't you?

80
00:05:37,840 --> 00:05:43,100
Maybe we should think of it as
just a regular rookie officer.

81
00:05:43,100 --> 00:05:43,900
Yeah.

82
00:05:45,200 --> 00:05:46,440
Alright, I get it.

83
00:05:47,120 --> 00:05:48,840
Whatever the latest model is,

84
00:05:48,840 --> 00:05:52,360
here you'll be treated as a rookie officer.

85
00:05:53,880 --> 00:05:55,040
Got a problem with that?

86
00:05:55,520 --> 00:05:57,380
It's not that, exactly.

87
00:05:57,380 --> 00:06:00,020
I'm your senior here.

88
00:06:00,020 --> 00:06:02,920
You were told to obey your seniors,
remember?

89
00:06:03,500 --> 00:06:05,380
Yes, understood, senior.

90
00:06:05,840 --> 00:06:07,220
Not senior.

91
00:06:07,220 --> 00:06:09,240
Call me "God."

92
00:06:09,240 --> 00:06:09,980
God?

93
00:06:10,700 --> 00:06:11,100
God?

94
00:06:12,300 --> 00:06:15,820
Whether you become a proper cop from now on

95
00:06:15,820 --> 00:06:17,460
depends on my training.

96
00:06:18,840 --> 00:06:20,480
Because I'm as good as a god!

97
00:06:21,600 --> 00:06:22,000
I see.

98
00:06:22,700 --> 00:06:24,320
Understood, God-chan.

99
00:06:25,860 --> 00:06:27,040
No need for the "chan."

100
00:06:27,040 --> 00:06:28,280
Yes, God.

101
00:06:29,320 --> 00:06:32,160
Good, that's settled. Let's go on patrol!

102
00:06:32,160 --> 00:06:33,740
Follow me, 004.

103
00:06:34,480 --> 00:06:35,600
Yes, God.

104
00:06:36,860 --> 00:06:40,140
Police box officers handle
directions and lost property

105
00:06:40,140 --> 00:06:44,280
and paperwork for thefts,
and they patrol to keep the peace.

106
00:06:44,280 --> 00:06:45,040
I see.

107
00:06:45,040 --> 00:06:50,140
It's important to always strive
to be loved by the residents.

108
00:06:50,140 --> 00:06:51,120
Meaning what?

109
00:06:52,140 --> 00:06:57,140
For example, like that, take the hand of an old
lady waiting at the signal and help her across.

110
00:06:57,140 --> 00:06:58,680
Yes, understood.

111
00:06:58,680 --> 00:06:59,560
Hey!

112
00:07:00,240 --> 00:07:02,220
Come on, let's cross together.

113
00:07:02,220 --> 00:07:04,040
Don't hold back.

114
00:07:04,040 --> 00:07:05,400
Help!

115
00:07:07,560 --> 00:07:08,860
Are you all right, granny?

116
00:07:10,780 --> 00:07:12,100
Ow ow!

117
00:07:12,100 --> 00:07:14,520
You idiot!
Are you trying to kill the old lady?

118
00:07:15,040 --> 00:07:21,800
I told you to look carefully!
The light's red! ...Oh, it really is.

119
00:07:22,380 --> 00:07:25,160
Honestly, pull yourself together. Sorry.

120
00:07:29,140 --> 00:07:31,540
Hey, you gonna fight or what?

121
00:07:31,540 --> 00:07:35,320
Oh no, it's a fight! I'm scared!

122
00:07:35,320 --> 00:07:42,680
Hey, this is no time to be scared! I'm bad at fights,
but stopping fights is part of a police officer's job!

123
00:07:42,680 --> 00:07:45,060
Police work?

124
00:07:45,500 --> 00:07:47,760
A robot can't lose to a human!

125
00:07:47,760 --> 00:07:49,560
Go, 004!

126
00:07:49,560 --> 00:07:51,620
Y-yes, God!

127
00:07:51,620 --> 00:07:53,920
Please stop!

128
00:07:53,920 --> 00:07:55,400
Come on, now's your chance!

129
00:07:55,400 --> 00:07:57,960
God, help me!

130
00:07:59,260 --> 00:08:01,440
He's really weak, isn't he?

131
00:08:02,260 --> 00:08:03,860
Hey, stop it!

132
00:08:07,800 --> 00:08:10,100
I'm really sorry, God.

133
00:08:10,620 --> 00:08:13,040
Show me you're good for something at least.

134
00:08:13,580 --> 00:08:14,460
I'll do my best.

135
00:08:15,080 --> 00:08:15,780
Yuji-chan!

136
00:08:17,460 --> 00:08:18,160
Get out!

137
00:08:18,160 --> 00:08:20,180
The child's -

138
00:08:20,180 --> 00:08:21,420
I'm standing right here.

139
00:08:22,240 --> 00:08:24,200
Scary, wait, 0045!

140
00:08:25,100 --> 00:08:26,820
I'm standing now, so don't worry.

141
00:08:29,700 --> 00:08:31,360
God, save me!

142
00:08:32,520 --> 00:08:34,160
If you can't swim, don't jump in!

143
00:08:39,500 --> 00:08:41,420
Thank goodness, Yuuji-chan.

144
00:08:42,160 --> 00:08:46,680
Honestly, why do humans have
to be the ones helping robots?

145
00:08:46,680 --> 00:08:47,840
It should be the other way around.

146
00:08:48,800 --> 00:08:50,700
Sorry, God.

147
00:08:50,700 --> 00:08:53,240
Get up, we're continuing the patrol.

148
00:08:54,440 --> 00:08:57,620
It seems water got in
and it can't move anymore.

149
00:08:57,620 --> 00:08:58,680
What?

150
00:09:01,500 --> 00:09:03,700
At least make it waterproof.

151
00:09:03,700 --> 00:09:06,300
What's so latest-model about this thing?

152
00:09:06,300 --> 00:09:08,920
Sorry, sorry.

153
00:09:11,400 --> 00:09:13,660
There, that should be fine now.

154
00:09:15,940 --> 00:09:19,020
Really? Thank you, God.

155
00:09:19,020 --> 00:09:22,880
Sorry, the truck's load collapsed.

156
00:09:23,680 --> 00:09:24,520
Whoa!

157
00:09:27,220 --> 00:09:30,860
Heavy lifting like this is exactly when a robot gets its chance,
Unit 0045.

158
00:09:31,420 --> 00:09:33,340
Yes, understood, God.

159
00:09:36,800 --> 00:09:38,340
Hang in there, Unit 0045!

160
00:09:38,340 --> 00:09:39,600
Come on, steady!

161
00:09:39,600 --> 00:09:41,920
Just a little more!

162
00:09:42,440 --> 00:09:47,040
Sorry, could I take a little break?

163
00:09:47,940 --> 00:09:49,780
Are you really a robot?

164
00:09:50,840 --> 00:09:53,240
Alright, second attempt!

165
00:09:54,660 --> 00:09:56,260
Almost there!

166
00:09:58,540 --> 00:09:59,500
We did it!

167
00:10:01,600 --> 00:10:02,700
Stop it!

168
00:10:06,820 --> 00:10:08,700
Help me, God!

169
00:10:09,300 --> 00:10:11,240
Don't add to our workload.

170
00:10:12,060 --> 00:10:13,600
I'm sorry.

171
00:10:15,340 --> 00:10:17,040
Good work, Ryo-chan.

172
00:10:17,040 --> 00:10:20,480
No stamina, zero athletic ability.

173
00:10:20,860 --> 00:10:23,340
On top of that,
he fails at everything he does.

174
00:10:24,520 --> 00:10:25,360
That's the kind of robot he is.

175
00:10:26,120 --> 00:10:27,040
Sorry.

176
00:10:27,900 --> 00:10:30,540
Everyone fails at first.

177
00:10:30,540 --> 00:10:32,600
Don't mope, just do your best.

178
00:10:34,100 --> 00:10:34,500
Thank you very much.

179
00:10:35,560 --> 00:10:36,780
I'll do my best.

180
00:10:40,080 --> 00:10:42,080
Oh no, I drank the tea.

181
00:10:42,080 --> 00:10:44,360
What do I do? The body looks lonely.

182
00:10:44,360 --> 00:10:46,560
Calm down and spit it out onto the handrail.

183
00:10:48,120 --> 00:10:50,400
Looks like this guy's name is settled.

184
00:10:54,520 --> 00:10:54,880
Well...

185
00:10:55,540 --> 00:10:58,540
Hey! He's a total Dame Taro!

186
00:10:59,720 --> 00:11:01,880
A total Dame Taro?

187
00:11:02,120 --> 00:11:03,040
Fits him perfectly, right?

188
00:11:03,840 --> 00:11:05,140
Dame Taro

189
00:11:07,940 --> 00:11:10,420
Robot Officer Dame Taro

190
00:11:13,340 --> 00:11:16,680
Hey, Dame Taro! We're heading out on patrol!

191
00:11:18,240 --> 00:11:19,320
Yes, God!

192
00:11:19,580 --> 00:11:21,280
Well, I'm off for a bit.

193
00:11:21,280 --> 00:11:22,320
Take care.

194
00:11:22,740 --> 00:11:23,540
Be careful!

195
00:11:24,520 --> 00:11:26,320
They make quite a good pair, don't they?

196
00:11:26,320 --> 00:11:30,280
Dame Taro's really settling in at this police box,
isn't he?

197
00:11:32,920 --> 00:11:34,980
Think I'll take a little break first.

198
00:11:41,660 --> 00:11:43,120
That looks tasty.

199
00:11:43,120 --> 00:11:45,760
If you drink it, you'll rust, you know.

200
00:11:45,760 --> 00:11:46,640
Yes.

201
00:11:47,540 --> 00:11:49,320
Don't make that pathetic face.

202
00:11:49,320 --> 00:11:51,980
I figured something like this might happen,

203
00:11:51,980 --> 00:11:55,400
so I got you this high-grade
lubricant for radio-controlled models.

204
00:11:55,920 --> 00:11:58,780
Wow, thank you so much, God!

205
00:11:59,200 --> 00:12:01,160
Drink it carefully, got it?

206
00:12:02,760 --> 00:12:05,300
You've got a pretty kind side after all,
Ryo-chan.

207
00:12:05,300 --> 00:12:08,520
It's Reiko. Coming back from shopping?

208
00:12:09,120 --> 00:12:10,740
Yes, good work, everyone.

209
00:12:11,380 --> 00:12:12,940
Are you two on patrol, Ryo-chan?

210
00:12:13,160 --> 00:12:15,500
Yeah, we're just taking a little break.

211
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:21,380
Officer, kick it!

212
00:12:23,180 --> 00:12:25,980
God, please let me handle this one.

213
00:12:27,440 --> 00:12:29,000
Alright, it's all yours.

214
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:30,840
Yes, here I go!

215
00:12:36,520 --> 00:12:38,300
That's not good, you two.

216
00:12:38,300 --> 00:12:40,340
What are you doing? That's not good.

217
00:12:42,880 --> 00:12:47,320
Honestly, it's like I've got a
completely useless little brother.

218
00:12:50,620 --> 00:12:57,500
Ohara-kun, about the robot police officer Unit 004 we were entrusted with,
have you heard?

219
00:12:58,860 --> 00:12:59,920
Heard what?

220
00:13:00,340 --> 00:13:05,760
Apparently the officers in the field have been calling it
"Dame Taro."

221
00:13:05,760 --> 00:13:10,600
Well, Unit 004 was
built by 2,000 researchers

222
00:13:10,600 --> 00:13:14,340
and 3,000 cutting-edge technologies.
Why would it get a nickname like that?

223
00:13:15,580 --> 00:13:20,080
I've looked over the duty reports,
and there seem to be quite a few mistakes.

224
00:13:20,600 --> 00:13:24,680
That's probably because Ryotsu is
blaming his own mistakes on Unit 004.

225
00:13:25,720 --> 00:13:31,760
No, apparently it's not only that. People
have actually seen Unit 004 make mistakes.

226
00:13:31,760 --> 00:13:37,940
Some have seen it. If this continues,
we ourselves will be held responsible!

227
00:13:38,980 --> 00:13:43,500
Do something about it, Ohara-kun.
Yes, sir... he's gone.

228
00:13:44,320 --> 00:13:52,020
Ryo-chan, Chief Ohara's waiting for you in the back.
Ugh, when that happens, it's never good news.

229
00:13:56,440 --> 00:13:57,880
What is it, Chief?

230
00:13:59,780 --> 00:14:00,880
It's a sickness.

231
00:14:02,060 --> 00:14:04,820
What did you do to Unit 004?

232
00:14:04,820 --> 00:14:06,480
W-what do you mean?

233
00:14:06,480 --> 00:14:11,460
Unit 004 is a robot built with
the finest of the latest technology!

234
00:14:11,460 --> 00:14:13,640
It can't possibly be useless.

235
00:14:13,640 --> 00:14:15,480
It must have gone that way
because you did something to it.

236
00:14:15,480 --> 00:14:17,000
I said, what did you do?

237
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:19,180
N-nothing! I didn't do anything!

238
00:14:19,860 --> 00:14:20,740
Don't lie.

239
00:14:20,740 --> 00:14:23,440
Then how did Unit 004 end up like that?

240
00:14:23,440 --> 00:14:25,840
It was like that from the start.

241
00:14:25,840 --> 00:14:27,060
Don't play dumb.

242
00:14:27,060 --> 00:14:29,440
You must have done something.

243
00:14:29,440 --> 00:14:31,340
Ja-ja-ja-jan, tabu-cha!

244
00:14:31,340 --> 00:14:33,920
An inspection from headquarters
is coming in three days.

245
00:14:33,920 --> 00:14:37,420
If Unit 004 doesn't show its
true capabilities at that time,

246
00:14:37,420 --> 00:14:39,540
you won't be getting a bonus.

247
00:14:39,540 --> 00:14:40,520
W-what, that's...

248
00:14:42,420 --> 00:14:45,860
If you don't want that, you'd better
get it back to normal within three days.

249
00:14:45,860 --> 00:14:47,220
That's unreasonable!

250
00:14:49,180 --> 00:14:51,820
If it can't perform properly in three days,

251
00:14:51,820 --> 00:14:55,200
what will happen to Dame Taro,
I mean Unit 004?

252
00:14:55,760 --> 00:14:58,640
If it's no use, we'll have no
choice but to take it back, right?

253
00:14:59,040 --> 00:15:02,360
Most likely, the only option
left is to scrap it, isn't it?

254
00:15:02,360 --> 00:15:06,440
Dame Taro gets scrapped?

255
00:15:13,400 --> 00:15:15,800
Ryo-chan, was that true just now?

256
00:15:17,060 --> 00:15:19,380
You two were listening?

257
00:15:19,380 --> 00:15:21,240
Don't tell me Dame Taro was too...

258
00:15:21,800 --> 00:15:22,460
It's fine.

259
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:24,900
Terai-san and I are heading to the station.

260
00:15:25,400 --> 00:15:26,020
I see.

261
00:15:26,500 --> 00:15:28,640
Is that really true, senpai?

262
00:15:29,060 --> 00:15:31,560
Dame Taro is going to be scrapped?

263
00:15:32,580 --> 00:15:35,000
In three days, an inspection
team from headquarters is coming,

264
00:15:35,540 --> 00:15:37,780
and if he's still useless by then,

265
00:15:38,960 --> 00:15:40,400
that's apparently what'll happen.

266
00:15:55,240 --> 00:15:57,620
I won't let them scrap him!

267
00:16:03,480 --> 00:16:05,320
Is this God's room?

268
00:16:06,020 --> 00:16:07,600
I'm going to put you to sleep for a bit.

269
00:16:08,600 --> 00:16:10,460
What are you doing, God?

270
00:16:16,840 --> 00:16:20,020
These are the Unit 004 blueprints
I got from Dr. Kubifuri.

271
00:16:20,460 --> 00:16:22,180
If it was built exactly according to these,

272
00:16:22,580 --> 00:16:25,520
it should be able to
perform beyond human strength,

273
00:16:25,900 --> 00:16:27,160
Let's take a look.

274
00:16:33,260 --> 00:16:34,520
There don't seem to be any abnormalities.

275
00:16:35,040 --> 00:16:38,700
Let's try raising the voltage a little.

276
00:16:41,440 --> 00:16:42,720
Alright, how about this?

277
00:16:44,660 --> 00:16:46,600
How do you feel, Dame Taro?

278
00:16:53,680 --> 00:16:55,620
Uh-oh, something's wrong.

279
00:17:02,060 --> 00:17:04,020
What? Receiving station, what's going on?

280
00:17:04,020 --> 00:17:04,780
What happened?

281
00:17:04,780 --> 00:17:06,820
Stop it, Dame Taro!

282
00:17:06,820 --> 00:17:12,400
Damn it,
the emergency stop switch is really here

283
00:17:13,780 --> 00:17:14,880
Aaaaaah!

284
00:17:17,020 --> 00:17:21,340
That was close.
Maybe the voltage was too high.

285
00:17:23,860 --> 00:17:25,160
How about now?

286
00:17:26,960 --> 00:17:32,080
How do you feel? Hopeless, right?
God, long time no see!

287
00:17:32,080 --> 00:17:36,280
Eeeeeeh!
You never come to visit me at all, you know.

288
00:17:36,880 --> 00:17:38,100
I've been so lonely!

289
00:17:41,880 --> 00:17:43,920
I know, I'll make some snacks.

290
00:17:43,920 --> 00:17:45,160
Here we go.

291
00:17:46,400 --> 00:17:48,320
It's gotten kind of feminine, hasn't it?

292
00:17:48,320 --> 00:17:50,060
Why did it turn out like that?

293
00:17:50,560 --> 00:17:53,300
But I have a feeling it'll be
much more useful than before.

294
00:17:55,600 --> 00:17:56,600
Spy!

295
00:17:56,600 --> 00:17:58,260
What about Miyanko?

296
00:17:58,460 --> 00:18:00,420
So it did end up being useful after all.

297
00:18:00,420 --> 00:18:00,920
Come on, come on.

298
00:18:00,920 --> 00:18:07,220
What should we do?

299
00:18:08,360 --> 00:18:09,980
If it's come to this,
we'll have to train it intensively.

300
00:18:13,960 --> 00:18:15,700
Look, your chin's up.

301
00:18:15,700 --> 00:18:17,020
Three more laps.

302
00:18:18,220 --> 00:18:18,580
Yes.

303
00:18:21,620 --> 00:18:23,940
Doing that to a robot is pointless.

304
00:18:23,940 --> 00:18:27,420
Well, it's not like it'll build muscle.

305
00:18:27,420 --> 00:18:30,100
No, it's actually quite meaningful.

306
00:18:31,420 --> 00:18:35,120
Dame Taro has the latest
learning function built in.

307
00:18:36,380 --> 00:18:38,680
So by accumulating experience,

308
00:18:39,080 --> 00:18:41,820
it learns more efficient
ways to move its body.

309
00:18:42,660 --> 00:18:46,540
As a result,
its performance should keep improving.

310
00:18:48,320 --> 00:18:49,220
I see.

311
00:18:50,040 --> 00:18:54,360
The problem is we only
have two days left, right?

312
00:18:55,900 --> 00:18:57,840
Look, your hips aren't in it.

313
00:18:59,380 --> 00:19:01,400
What are you doing? It's like this, right?

314
00:19:03,420 --> 00:19:05,000
Come on, another 100 reps.

315
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:09,360
Swim faster if you don't want to rust.

316
00:19:09,360 --> 00:19:12,480
Are you even trying?

317
00:19:16,280 --> 00:19:17,600
200 more reps.

318
00:19:20,820 --> 00:19:21,920
It's me.

319
00:19:22,500 --> 00:19:23,920
What? The Chief?

320
00:19:23,920 --> 00:19:25,860
Got it, I'll be right back.

321
00:19:27,020 --> 00:19:29,180
I'm heading back to the station for a bit.

322
00:19:29,180 --> 00:19:31,960
Make sure you finish the remaining 200 reps.

323
00:19:31,960 --> 00:19:32,540
Yes.

324
00:19:34,760 --> 00:19:35,200
Good.

325
00:19:36,100 --> 00:19:37,860
It's out of battery.

326
00:19:43,360 --> 00:19:44,980
Nobody's here.

327
00:19:46,300 --> 00:19:49,360
I'll just borrow a bit of charge.

328
00:19:49,360 --> 00:19:49,520
Mm.

329
00:19:50,500 --> 00:19:50,940
Mm.

330
00:19:52,440 --> 00:19:52,880
Mm.

331
00:19:56,120 --> 00:19:58,240
What? It's today?

332
00:19:59,440 --> 00:20:00,940
It's God's voice!

333
00:20:02,300 --> 00:20:05,200
The inspection was supposed to be in two days,
wasn't it?

334
00:20:05,620 --> 00:20:08,540
Because of the magazine launch,
it was suddenly moved up.

335
00:20:09,240 --> 00:20:09,600
No way.

336
00:20:09,600 --> 00:20:13,620
Whether the day after tomorrow becomes today won't make much difference,
will it?

337
00:20:14,240 --> 00:20:17,480
Or are you plotting something sinister?

338
00:20:17,960 --> 00:20:19,440
No, senpai is -

339
00:20:20,420 --> 00:20:22,120
Please, just wait a little longer.

340
00:20:23,100 --> 00:20:25,460
We don't want to scrap Dame Taro.

341
00:20:26,700 --> 00:20:29,760
M-me, scrap...

342
00:20:31,280 --> 00:20:32,200
Ryotsu

343
00:20:35,860 --> 00:20:37,360
Yes, this is Ohara.

344
00:20:38,680 --> 00:20:40,100
Understood.

345
00:20:41,960 --> 00:20:44,180
The inspection is apparently coming soon.

346
00:20:45,220 --> 00:20:46,020
Damn it!

347
00:20:46,020 --> 00:20:47,040
Ryo-chan.

348
00:20:47,040 --> 00:20:47,820
Senpai.

349
00:20:48,260 --> 00:20:49,740
Eeeh?

350
00:20:50,620 --> 00:20:51,880
Tetetetete...

351
00:20:51,880 --> 00:20:54,560
Who left their clothes in a place like this?

352
00:20:55,460 --> 00:20:57,020
These are Dame Taro's clothes!

353
00:20:57,620 --> 00:21:00,000
Don't tell me you were
listening to that conversation...

354
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:01,360
Dame Taro!

355
00:21:09,220 --> 00:21:11,140
Sayōnara!

356
00:21:12,860 --> 00:21:15,660
Even though you were born
as a robot police officer,

357
00:21:16,160 --> 00:21:19,160
to be scrapped before you've
been of any use at all!

358
00:21:32,100 --> 00:21:33,320
There are people still inside.

359
00:21:35,080 --> 00:21:36,660
You'll get caught in the explosion!

360
00:21:38,900 --> 00:21:39,800
I can't run away.

361
00:21:39,800 --> 00:21:41,660
I'm a police officer.

362
00:21:48,680 --> 00:21:49,180
You...

363
00:21:50,340 --> 00:21:52,940
Robot police officer prototype, Unit 004,

364
00:21:52,940 --> 00:21:54,700
Otsugata, the totally useless Dame Taro.

365
00:21:56,940 --> 00:21:57,420
This is...

366
00:21:57,420 --> 00:21:59,440
Not good enough, is it?

367
00:22:00,520 --> 00:22:02,720
God, please accept this.

368
00:22:06,940 --> 00:22:09,680
That won't do!
You too, get out of here quick!

369
00:22:10,380 --> 00:22:10,860
Yes.

370
00:22:14,520 --> 00:22:16,700
What are you doing? Hurry up!

371
00:22:16,700 --> 00:22:17,740
That won't do, you!

372
00:22:21,680 --> 00:22:23,080
That won't do!

373
00:22:27,640 --> 00:22:28,800
That won't do!

374
00:22:30,160 --> 00:22:34,060
Pull yourself together, that won't do!

375
00:22:34,060 --> 00:22:39,340
I've finally been able
to be of use to people.

376
00:22:39,340 --> 00:22:42,360
You're a fine police officer.

377
00:22:43,500 --> 00:22:46,360
I've had so much fun until now.

378
00:22:47,080 --> 00:22:52,100
Thank you so much, God.

379
00:22:54,300 --> 00:22:55,740
Hey, what are you saying?

380
00:22:55,740 --> 00:22:57,800
No, no, that won't do!

381
00:23:01,120 --> 00:23:02,500
That won't do!

382
00:23:11,440 --> 00:23:14,560
Thanks to you, it didn't get scrapped.

383
00:23:15,420 --> 00:23:18,060
After all,
it saved the Police Commissioner General.

384
00:23:18,520 --> 00:23:19,320
Of course.

385
00:23:20,060 --> 00:23:22,680
As expected of the latest model robot cop.

386
00:23:23,080 --> 00:23:27,760
It's no wonder, since it absorbed 2,000
researchers and 3,000 cutting-edge technologies.

387
00:23:28,140 --> 00:23:31,920
If it couldn't move because the battery died,
you should have said so from the start.

388
00:23:31,920 --> 00:23:35,000
Well, if it couldn't move,
it couldn't talk either.

389
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:35,640
Hmph.

390
00:23:36,320 --> 00:23:38,060
Ryo-chan, you're happy, aren't you?

391
00:23:38,060 --> 00:23:41,880
Honestly,
I've never seen a senior like that before.

392
00:23:42,300 --> 00:23:44,420
What did you do, God?

393
00:23:44,920 --> 00:23:45,780
Nothing!

394
00:23:46,220 --> 00:23:49,380
You're still not a full-fledged officer,
you know.

395
00:23:50,000 --> 00:23:53,020
From now on, I'll whip you into shape.

396
00:23:53,020 --> 00:23:54,040
Whoa.

397
00:23:54,470 --> 00:23:54,900
Wait!

398
00:23:55,740 --> 00:23:56,760
Ow

399
00:23:56,760 --> 00:24:00,120
Idiot, is there anyone who
runs straight out into the road?

400
00:24:00,120 --> 00:24:02,140
But God...

401
00:24:20,020 --> 00:24:27,460
I probably don't want to become
someone who plays silly games with looks.

402
00:24:27,460 --> 00:24:34,400
If I'm dawdling at the street corner,
the moon slips away.

403
00:24:34,400 --> 00:24:42,620
Right now isn't everything,
so don't push yourself too hard.

404
00:24:42,620 --> 00:24:46,360
Even if you cheat a little with a lie,

405
00:24:46,360 --> 00:24:50,520
once in a while, while helping someone.

406
00:24:50,520 --> 00:24:53,545
Baby, do you know me?

407
00:24:53,595 --> 00:24:54,620
Toward tomorrow,

408
00:24:54,620 --> 00:24:56,860
a nice spirit.

409
00:24:58,040 --> 00:25:01,880
Don't rot away, we'll do what needs doing.

410
00:25:01,880 --> 00:25:04,360
A cute spirit.

411
00:25:04,360 --> 00:25:07,780
What's hard to understand is

412
00:25:08,780 --> 00:25:11,200
wanting to look that way.

413
00:25:13,200 --> 00:25:17,440
Better than a makeover, right?

414
00:25:19,340 --> 00:25:24,480
Wh-wh-what... what... what...

415
00:25:30,020 --> 00:25:32,420
We meet again, Professor Tondemo!

416
00:25:32,420 --> 00:25:34,920
What? A potion to make me invisible?

417
00:25:34,920 --> 00:25:38,280
Who'd ever help with a
human experiment like that?

418
00:25:38,280 --> 00:25:41,860
Wait, when did I turn
invisible without me noticing?!

419
00:25:42,620 --> 00:25:44,260
Damn it! You tricked me!

420
00:25:44,580 --> 00:25:47,900
Next time: Invisible data appears!
See you then!

421
00:25:48,820 --> 00:25:50,820
There's a wall over there!

422
00:25:52,040 --> 00:25:54,060
Well, there's probably a wall too!

423
00:25:55,500 --> 00:25:59,260
Everybody, come on over to our town!

424
00:26:00,320 --> 00:26:00,860
Thank you!

